    "# Lab 8 (Lecture 30): Gold-Standard Construction, NIST ASR Evaluation & Bootstrap Confidence Intervals\n",
    "**Course:** CIS 531/731: Programming Techniques for Data Science and Analytics (Fall 2026)  \n",
    "**Date:** Friday, November 6, 2026  \n",
    "**Phase 5:** Evaluate & Deploy | **Module 9:** Evaluating Models: Inferential Statistics & ASR Evaluation  \n",
    "**Culminates In:** Problem Set 8 (PS 8), Machine Problem 9 (MP 9), and HW 12 Final Term-Project Evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Lab Objectives\n",
    "In Lectures 28 and 29, we established two foundational laws of defensible data science:\n",
    "1. **A point estimate without a confidence interval is mathematically invalid** (Lecture 28). Every reported Macro-F1 score, Word Error Rate (WER), or generational drift trajectory must be accompanied by a **95% Non-Parametric Percentile Bootstrap Confidence Interval** (B = 1000).\n",
    "2. **An evaluation is only as valid as the ground truth it is measured against** (Lecture 29 & 30). Using an LLM (e.g., GPT/Claude) or an ASR model (e.g., Whisper Large) to generate your reference test set introduces **methodological circularity**—measuring model agreement rather than true accuracy.\n",
    "\n",
    "In this execution lab, you will:\n",
    "1. **Enforce Course Invariant INV-17 & The Annotation Cap:** Draw a stratified sample capped at **N <= 50 objects (or <= 2 hours of human annotation labor)** and log human-verified ground truth (source=\"gold\").\n",
    "2. **Implement a NIST OpenASR Transcript Normalization Pipeline:** Standardize casing, punctuation, digit-to-word expansion, and disfluencies (<hesitation>) so acoustic accuracy is never confounded with formatting.\n",
    "3. **Compute Exact Levenshtein Alignment, Word Error Rate (WER), & Entity Error Rate (EER):** Extract exact Substitution (S), Deletion (D), Insertion (I), and Correct (C) counts, and measure domain-specific Named Entity preservation.\n",
    "4. **Bridge ASR to Downstream Trope Classification (Lab 6 Integration):** Evaluate a Baseline vs. Alternative classifier on your human gold set using scikit-learn.\n",
    "5. **Construct 95% Percentile Bootstrap Confidence Intervals (B = 1000):** Quantify uncertainty on WER, Macro-F1, paired model differences (ΔF1 = F1_alt - F1_base), and stratified generational cohort drift."
   ]
  },
