    "## Part 1: Environment Setup, Stratified Sampling & The Gold-Standard Schema (INV-17)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Architectural Rules for Gold-Standard Construction\n",
    "* **INV-17 (Human Ground-Truth Mandate):** Every transcript reference (`gold_transcript`) and thematic label (`gold_trope`) in your gold evaluation split **must** be authored by a human student (`source=\"gold\"`). Never use LLM pseudo-labels as ground truth in your evaluation split.\n",
    "* **Thermal Load & Annotation Cap:** Individual annotation for this lab and MP 9 is strictly capped at **N <= 50 items or <= 2 hours of human effort**. For 2–3 person teams, pooled gold sets in HW 12 must contain **50–200 items**.\n",
    "* **Stratified Sampling Across Cohorts/Conditions:** Never annotate only the first 5 minutes of a broadcast or a single decade. Sample across temporal cohorts (`1990s`–`2020s`) or acoustic conditions (`clean_studio`, `noisy_caller`, `music_bed`) so your 50-item gold set captures the true variance of the corpus."
   ]
  },
