    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Part 2: NIST OpenASR Transcript Normalization & Disfluency Protocol\n",
    "Per **Lecture 29 (Slides 4–6)**, calculating Word Error Rate (WER) on unnormalized text is scientifically invalid because capitalization (\"The\" vs. \"the\"), punctuation (\"forever,\" vs. \"forever\"), numeral formatting (\"5\" vs. \"five\"), and spontaneous speech disfluencies (\"um\", \"uh\", \"er\") artificially inflate Substitution (S) and Deletion (D) counts.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Our Explicit Normalization Rules (NIST OpenASR Compliant)\n",
    "1. **Lowercase Conversion:** Map all characters to lowercase.\n",
    "2. **Digit-to-Spoken-Word Expansion:** Map numerals (0–10, 21, 6th, 7th, 1994, 2004, 2024, etc.) to their canonical spoken English tokens.\n",
    "3. **Disfluency & Hesitation Protocol:** Map spontaneous hesitation tokens (um, uh, er, ah, hmm) to a canonical `<hesitation>` marker or strip them deterministically from **both** the reference and the hypothesis (needed when evaluating Whisper models that auto-filter filler words).\n",
    "4. **Punctuation Stripping & Whitespace Collapse:** Replace non-alphanumeric punctuation with spaces and collapse consecutive whitespace."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "DIGIT_MAP = {\n",
    "    \"0\": \"zero\",\n",
    "    \"1\": \"one\",\n",
    "    \"2\": \"two\",\n",
    "    \"3\": \"three\",\n",
    "    \"4\": \"four\",\n",
    "    \"5\": \"five\",\n",
    "    \"6\": \"six\",\n",
    "    \"6th\": \"sixth\",\n",
    "    \"7\": \"seven\",\n",
    "    \"7th\": \"seventh\",\n",
    "    \"8\": \"eight\",\n",
    "    \"9\": \"nine\",\n",
    "    \"10\": \"ten\",\n",
    "    \"21\": \"twenty one\",\n",
    "    \"1994\": \"nineteen ninety four\",\n",
    "    \"2004\": \"two thousand four\",\n",
    "    \"2024\": \"twenty twenty four\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "HESITATION_TOKENS = {\"um\", \"uh\", \"er\", \"ah\", \"hmm\", \"uhh\", \"umm\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "def normalize_nist_transcript(text: str, hesitation_mode: str = \"strip\") -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Applies NIST OpenASR normalization rules to a reference or hypothesis string.\n",
    "    hesitation_mode: 'strip' (removes filler words) or 'tag' (maps to <hesitation>).\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    t = text.lower()\n",
    "    # Strip non-alphanumeric punctuation without backslash escape collisions\n",
    "    t = re.sub(r\"[^a-zA-Z0-9 ]\", \" \", t)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    raw_tokens = t.split()\n",
    "    norm_tokens = []\n",
    "    for tok in raw_tokens:\n",
    "        if tok in HESITATION_TOKENS:\n",
    "            if hesitation_mode == \"tag\":\n",
    "                norm_tokens.append(\"<hesitation>\")\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        if tok in DIGIT_MAP:\n",
    "            norm_tokens.extend(DIGIT_MAP[tok].split())\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            norm_tokens.append(tok)\n",
    "            \n",
    "    return \" \".join(norm_tokens)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply NIST normalization across Gold Reference, Baseline ASR, and Alternative ASR\n",
    "df_gold[\"norm_gold\"] = df_gold[\"gold_transcript\"].apply(lambda s: normalize_nist_transcript(s, \"strip\"))\n",
    "df_gold[\"norm_asr_base\"] = df_gold[\"asr_base_hyp\"].apply(lambda s: normalize_nist_transcript(s, \"strip\"))\n",
    "df_gold[\"norm_asr_alt\"] = df_gold[\"asr_alt_hyp\"].apply(lambda s: normalize_nist_transcript(s, \"strip\"))\n",
